WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.180
A kilogram of uranium-235,
fully fissioned,

2
00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.050
releases about 2 million times the
energy of a kilogram of car fuel.

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.640
Fuel burns using energy
stored in chemical bonds.

4
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.110
Uranium's comes from the nucleus.

5
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.780
Electric cars store their
energy in batteries instead.

6
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:22.610
Yet a car's battery is far
heavier than a tank of fuel.

7
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.860
Why must an electric car carry
so much more mass of battery?

8
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.910
In this mission, you'll compare how
much energy each kilogram holds,

9
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.990
from wood to hydrogen.

10
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.870
Then you'll weigh up chemical cells and
solar cells as sources for a circuit.

11
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.850
Your mission: explain why an electric
car must carry far more mass of battery

12
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.480
than a fuel-burning car carries in fuel.
